cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "INA-sim: a traceable ice nucleation screening lab"
message: >-
  If you use INA-sim in work you publish, please cite it, and cite the
  underlying parameterizations directly — every number this tool reports names
  its own source, and those sources deserve the credit. Run `ina-sim refs` for
  the full bibliography with DOIs.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Hearn
    given-names: Christian Thomas
repository-code: "https://github.com/HearnChristian/ina-sim"
abstract: >-
  A local, offline screening tool for ice nucleating agents. It separates a
  heuristic ranking layer from an empirical layer of published ice nucleation
  active site density parameterizations, each carried with its units, surface
  area basis, fitted temperature range, stated uncertainty and DOI. The tool
  refuses to extrapolate beyond a source's fitted range, refuses to compare
  values measured on different surface area bases, and re-derives the published
  claims it depends on as part of its test suite. It imports droplet-freezing
  experiments, propagates uncertainty by Monte Carlo, and records every run in a
  hash-chained audit log.
keywords:
  - ice-nucleation
  - atmospheric-science
  - cloud-seeding
  - weather-modification
  - reproducible-research
license: MIT
